# Trivy Vulnerability Ignore File
# This file contains vulnerabilities that are being intentionally ignored
# Each entry should include a comment explaining why it's safe to ignore

# ==================== POLICY ====================
# GitHub workflows enforce: CRITICAL,HIGH severity only
# See: .github/actions/trivy-scan/action.yml
#
# MEDIUM and LOW severity vulnerabilities do not block CI/CD and
# should NOT be added to this file unless there is a specific reason
# to suppress them from local development scans.

# ==================== EXAMPLE FORMAT ====================
# CVE-YYYY-XXXXX - Brief description
# Affects: package-name version
# Severity: CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW
# Issue: Detailed description of vulnerability
# Risk: Analysis of actual risk in this context
# Status: Fixed in version X.Y.Z / No fix available (affected)
# Reason: Why it's safe to ignore (false positive, not applicable, etc.)
# Review: When to re-evaluate this decision
# CVE-YYYY-XXXXX

# ==================== ACTIVE IGNORES ====================

# ==================================================================
# Inherited from UBI9 base image (ai-assistant-home)
# ==================================================================
# These three CVEs come from the parent ai-assistant-home image and have
# no fix in RHEL 9 yet (Red Hat published fixes only for "Hardened Images",
# not standard UBI9). Project-container inherits them; the upstream
# image/.trivyignore documents the full risk reasoning.
#
# Same risk story applies in your customized container: non-root runtime,
# firewall-restricted egress, no DTLS surface, no GSSAPI accept side, and
# no NegoEx mechanism registered. If your project legitimately introduces
# any of those (e.g., adding a Kerberos auth flow), re-triage these before
# keeping the suppression.

# CVE-2026-33845 - GnuTLS DTLS handshake integer underflow [NO FIX AVAILABLE]
# Affects: gnutls-3.8.3-10.el9_7 (UBI9 base, transitive)
# Risk: LOW — no DTLS surface in container; gnutls is transitive, not invoked
# Status: ACTIVE - No RHEL 9 errata. Suppressed in upstream image/.trivyignore.
# Review: Patch within 30 days of RHEL 9 errata, or re-evaluate by 2026-08-04
CVE-2026-33845

# CVE-2026-33846 - GnuTLS DTLS handshake heap buffer overflow [NO FIX AVAILABLE]
# Affects: gnutls-3.8.3-10.el9_7 (UBI9 base, transitive)
# Risk: LOW — no DTLS surface in container; gnutls is transitive, not invoked
# Status: ACTIVE - No RHEL 9 errata. Suppressed in upstream image/.trivyignore.
# Review: Patch within 30 days of RHEL 9 errata, or re-evaluate by 2026-08-04
CVE-2026-33846

# CVE-2026-40356 - MIT krb5 NegoEx integer underflow [NO FIX AVAILABLE]
# Affects: krb5-libs-1.21.1-9.el9_7 (UBI9 base, transitive via openssh-clients)
# Risk: LOW — no GSSAPI server, NegoEx not registered in /etc/gss/mech
# Status: ACTIVE - No RHEL 9 errata. Suppressed in upstream image/.trivyignore.
# Review: Patch within 30 days of RHEL 9 errata, or re-evaluate by 2026-08-04
CVE-2026-40356

# ==================== NOTES ====================
# This is the starter template for new project containers based on
# ai-assistant-home (UBI9 minimal). When you customize your container,
# review scan results and add entries here only for CRITICAL/HIGH
# vulnerabilities that need to be suppressed with documented justification.
#
# If you install skopeo from RHEL repos: expect 5+ HIGH CVEs from its
# bundled Go stdlib. RHEL marks them will_not_fix or has no scheduled
# rebuild; this is expected to clear up when ai-assistant-home migrates
# to UBI10. See the upstream project-container .trivyignore for reference
# suppressions and an explanation of why the upstream-skopeo binary swap
# fails on UBI9:
# https://github.com/rise8-us/xpai-ai-assistant-container/blob/main/project-container/.trivyignore
#
# If you install gh (GitHub CLI) or other Go-based tools: expect Go stdlib
# CVEs from their embedded Go runtimes. Triage each on its own merits.

# Last reviewed: 2026-05-06
